# Markup Tool

`GET /admin/toolbox/markup` renders `templates/markup.html`, a standalone full-screen page for all logged-in users. It does not extend `base.html` so the canvas can own the viewport and touch gestures.

## Frontend

- Engine: Konva from CDN, `perfect-freehand` from jsDelivr via **non-blocking** dynamic `import()` (never block init on external ESM), `idb-keyval` from CDN. There is no bundler.
- Layers: background images (`bgLayer`), drawing nodes (`drawLayer`), selection UI (`uiLayer`).
- Infinite canvas = stage position + scale. One pointer draws; two pointers pan/pinch-zoom. Hand tool pans with one pointer.
- Tools: pen, highlighter, stroke eraser, lasso select/move/delete, text, line/rect/ellipse. Pen and highlighter keep independent size/color settings; lock-size starts enabled. Highlighter defaults to a larger yellow-first palette. Brush size auto-defaults relative to the first imported image (`autoConfigureSizes`); the size slider shows a live on-screen preview circle (`showSizePreview`).
- Eraser and lasso must hit-test **actual geometry**, not bounding boxes: eraser uses point-to-segment / shape-outline distance (`eraserHitsNode`); lasso uses `nodeIntersectsPolygon` and supports tap-to-select. Stroke selections draw a dashed highlight rect (`updateSelectionRect`); image-only selections use the Konva `Transformer` with resize anchors (`syncSelectionUi`, `selectionIsImageOnly`).
- Snap mode shows a grey preview after the hold threshold, then replaces held pen strokes with recognized perfect shapes on release. `buildSnappedShape` chooses the better fit of rectangle vs ellipse (compare `rectangleScore` vs `ellipseScore`) so squares stay squares and circles stay circles; it returns `null` (keep freehand) when neither fits.
- Undo/redo is operation-based (`add`, `remove`, `modify`) using serialized Konva node attrs.
- Local autosave uses IndexedDB key `oqb:markup:autosave:v1`; no server-side persistence. Saves are debounced (400 ms) and serialized (`saveInFlight`); `readAutosave()` waits for pending writes and times out after 5 s so rapid mobile reload cannot hang init. Flushes on tab close/hide. On load, if a non-empty autosave exists, show the restore card **before** loading any `?img=` / share-target import — user picks **Restore** or **Start new**.
- Imported background images live on `bgLayer`, are listening-enabled, and can be selected/moved/resized/deleted with the lasso tool (tap or loop-select; resize via transformer handles when image-only selection).
- Imports are **resolution-normalized** in `loadBackgroundImage`: the node's world width/height are scaled so the longest edge maps to `MARKUP_NORMALIZED_MAX_DIM` (default 2400 world units; super-admin tunable via **Admin → System Settings → Markup**), regardless of source pixel size. This keeps the fit zoom level and pen-size scale consistent for tiny and huge images. The full-res source `img` is still drawn (export quality preserved). `autoConfigureSizes(maxWorldDim)` derives default pen/highlighter sizes from the normalized world dimension.
- Export (`exportMarkup`) computes a union bounding box over image + drawing nodes via `contentBounds()`, then renders the crop directly from the live stage (save transform → reset to identity → add a white background rect → hide `uiLayer` → `stage.toDataURL({x,y,width,height})` → restore), and shares/downloads a cropped PNG. Do **not** call `node.isDestroyed()` (not a function on Konva nodes in this build) — use `node.getLayer()` truthiness to test attachment.

## Imports

- Android share target: service worker stores the POSTed image in Cache API (`markup-share-v1`, `/__oqb_markup_shared_image__`), then opens `?shared=1`.
- Upload/paste: **Import** opens `#importBackdrop` with file picker, **Paste from clipboard** (`readClipboardAsImageBlob`: `clipboard.read()` image types, else `readText` + base64), and a tap-to-paste zone. Global paste still works on the canvas.
- iOS Share Shortcut: `GET /admin/toolbox/markup/ios-shortcut.shortcut` + `?ios-share=paste` (opens import sheet in share mode) or `?ios-share=hash#…` (inline base64). Prefer signed file at `static/markup/Markup-OQB-signed.shortcut` when available — iOS 15+ rejects unsigned downloads.
- Present mode: `templates/viewer.html` opens `/admin/toolbox/markup?img=<same-origin-url>` for IMG assets or DOC thumbnails. MD assets have no image URL and should not show a Markup button.
- Reject external `?img=` URLs to avoid canvas-tainting export failures.

## PWA

`app/pwa.py` serves `/manifest.webmanifest` and `/sw.js` from `static/markup/`. Keep `/sw.js` root-scoped with `Service-Worker-Allowed: /` so Web Share Target POSTs can be intercepted.

Android Chrome supports installed-PWA Web Share Target. iOS Safari does not; iOS must use installed PWA + upload/paste, with Shortcuts only as a documented workaround.

When not in standalone mode, show floating `#installInfoBtn` (bottom-right). It opens `#installHelpBackdrop` with platform-highlighted instructions (`detectInstallPlatform`, `isStandaloneApp`). Hide the button once installed (`display-mode: standalone` or `navigator.standalone`).

**iOS Share Shortcut (PairDrop-style):** `GET /admin/toolbox/markup/ios-shortcut.shortcut` (`build_ios_share_shortcut` in `app/toolbox/markup.py`) generates an unsigned Shortcuts action extension: convert image → JPEG, base64 encode, copy to clipboard, open `{base}/admin/toolbox/markup?ios-share=paste`. That URL opens `#importBackdrop` in share mode; paste uses `readClipboardAsImageBlob` (image blob or base64 text). Also supports `?ios-share=hash#BASE64` for small images. iOS share import skips the autosave-restore prompt. Unsigned files fail on iOS 15+ unless replaced by `Markup-OQB-signed.shortcut` or imported via `shortcuts://import-shortcut/?url=…`.
